{
  "title": "iOS has no bulk import (Paprika archive)",
  "description": "Web has a full import flow \
(ramekin-ui/src/pages/ImportPage.tsx + ramekin-ui/src/utils/paprikaImport.ts) \
that parses .paprikarecipes archives client-side, extracts photos, and pushes \
recipes via ImportApi. iOS never calls any ImportAPI method — there is no \
import UI at all.\n\
\n\
Add a Paprika archive import flow to iOS: pick the archive via the document \
picker, parse (gzip-per-recipe inside a zip — mirror the logic in \
paprikaImport.ts), and submit through the generated ImportAPI, with progress \
and per-recipe error reporting consistent with how web handles it.\n\
\n\
Worth considering as part of implementation: if client-side archive parsing in \
Swift is painful, evaluate moving archive parsing server-side so both clients \
just upload the file — that would delete the web-side parsing code too and \
prevent future drift (see p3-shared-client-business-logic-strategy).",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 2,
  "type": "task",
